# Dependencies. NEVER commit these.
#
# This file used to contain ONLY the .env rules below. It got rsynced over the
# deploy repo's real .gitignore, and the next `git add -A` swept node_modules into
# the commit. node_modules holds binaries far over GitHub's 100 MB file limit (the
# Next SWC binary alone is ~116 MB), so the push was rejected outright. Keep this
# list complete: this file is synced, so a gap here silently breaks the repo.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Build output
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Secrets. Never commit.
.env*
!.env*.example

# 🔴 THE HMRC SANDBOX SESSION. It looks like config and it is a credential file.
#
# scripts/hmrc-sandbox-demo.mjs writes the live sandbox session into it: a server token, an access
# token, a refresh token, and the HMRC issued test user's own id, password, National Insurance
# number and UTR. It was tracked from the beginning and went up with every push, because "sandbox"
# reads as "not real" and a .json in the repo root reads as settings.
#
# They are test credentials, not production ones, and the repo is private. It is still a live
# session for an HMRC service sitting in git history, and we are in the middle of an HMRC
# production approval whose checklist asks how we handle exactly this.
.hmrc-sandbox.json

# Vercel
.vercel

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# Testing
coverage/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
*.pem
.idea/
.vscode/

# Orphaned file handles from the Cowork FUSE mount, and 0 byte editor temp files.
# They are not source. They got committed once; never again.
.fuse_hidden*
XX*
